    "INTRODUCTION",
    "At 9 a.m., Old Cairo is still waking up. Vendors set out their wares in front of shops while young delivery guys zip past on bikes balancing racks of aish baladi, local flatbread, on their heads. Imposing gates punctuate the walls surrounding the neighborhood; during the Middle Ages, the sultan ordered them closed to keep the Crusaders out. But these days, the gates to the ancient core of the city stay open to all. At this hour, the sun isn’t too strong, and traffic hasn’t yet reached peak chaos. So I go with my chef buddy Moustafa Elrefaey to hit up one of our favorite ful carts."
